Article 4: Where the amount of money laundered is five million yuan or more, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in Article 191 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Committing money laundering acts on multiple occasions;
(2) Refusing to cooperate with the recovery of property, resulting in the inability to recover the illicit proceeds and the proceeds generated therefrom;
(3) Causing losses of two hundred fifty thousand yuan or more;
(4) Causing other serious consequences.
Where a person commits money laundering criminal acts on two or more occasions and should have been subject to criminal punishment according to law but has not yet been dealt with, the amount of money laundered shall be calculated cumulatively.

Article 5: Where, for the purpose of concealing or disguising the source and nature of the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom derived from the commission of any predicate offense as prescribed in Article 191 of the Criminal Law, a person commits any of the following acts, such act may be deemed as "concealing or disguising the source and nature of the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom by other methods" as provided in Item (5) of the first paragraph of Article 191 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Transferring or converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom through means such as pawn, lease, sale, investment, auction, or purchase of financial products;
(2) Transferring or converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom by mixing them with the business income of cash-intensive venues such as shopping malls, restaurants, and entertainment venues;
(3) Transferring or converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom through fictitious transactions, fictitious creditor's rights and debts, false guarantees, false income declarations, etc.;
(4) Converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom through means such as purchasing lottery tickets, prize coupons, stored-value cards, gold and other precious metals;
(5) Converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom into gambling proceeds through gambling;
(6) Transferring or converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom through transactions in "virtual assets" or exchange of financial assets;
(7) Transferring or converting the proceeds and proceeds generated therefrom by other methods.

Article 7: The determination of the crime of money laundering shall be based on the premise that the predicate offense is established. The existence of any of the following circumstances shall not affect the determination of the crime of money laundering:
(1) The predicate offense has not yet been adjudicated according to law, but there is evidence proving that it actually exists;
(2) There is evidence proving that the predicate offense actually exists, but the perpetrator has absconded and is not yet brought to justice;
(3) There is evidence proving that the predicate offense actually exists, but due to the death of the perpetrator or other reasons, criminal liability is not investigated according to law;
(4) There is evidence proving that the predicate offense actually exists, but the perpetrator is convicted and punished for another crime because the act also constitutes another crime.
